From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:11:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qwen27: a shared round's MTP chains draft together, one frame
 a step

A shared round drafted each stream's MTP chain in turn, one GPU frame per
draft, and each frame's single-row attention ran 16 threadgroups, so four
chats spent about 12 ms a round drafting against a 9 ms verify of all their
rows. The chains now step together: one frame drafts the next token of every
chain still going, and their attentions run as one, keys side by side under a
per-row mask (the head's own 4-window attention). The slots' early taps gathers
share one pass. A lone chain takes the same kernels and mask as before.

M5 Ultra, Qwen3.5-9B q4, served greedy, drafted / "draft": false, every reply
token-identical: 4 chats x 1K 303 -> 364 tok/s aggregate (plain 306), drafting
12.6 -> 7.7 ms a round before the shared gather; one chat 1K 228, 4K 197, 8K 203, 32K 171, re-quote
1,015, code edit 451, story 213, as before.
